Reviewing my own run, two shortcomings recur with verbatim support, one candidate rule lacks verbatim grounding, and one is malformed.

```json
[
  {
    "id": "emit-parseable-output-block-first",
    "type": "harness-rule",
    "trigger": {
      "family": ["lna"],
      "analysis": ["generation"],
      "failure_signature": ["move-repertoire"],
      "keywords": ["netlist", "parse", "output-contract", "narrowband", "nf", "s11"]
    },
    "evidence": [
      {"quote": "model emitted no parseable netlist block", "source": "my trajectory rows, roundtrip phase"}
    ],
    "rule": "Always emit the fenced netlist block in the exact contracted shape before anything else, since a candidate with no parseable block is discarded before it can be sized.",
    "applicability": {
      "applies": "Every propose and edit turn where I must return a netlist.",
      "not": "Turns that only diagnose and are not expected to return a netlist."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "vary-topology-after-hard-failure",
    "type": "strategy",
    "trigger": {
      "family": ["lna"],
      "analysis": ["generation"],
      "failure_signature": ["topology-exhaustion"],
      "keywords": ["topology", "escalation", "hard-failure", "diversity"]
    },
    "evidence": [
      {"quote": "HARD FAILURE after escalation; infeasible (closest attempt saved)", "source": "my results notes"}
    ],
    "rule": "After a hard failure survives escalation, change the topology class on the next attempt rather than re-proposing the same archetype that already hard-failed.",
    "applicability": {
      "applies": "Specs that remained infeasible after the escalation retry.",
      "not": "Specs that reached feasible at base, where topology variation is unnecessary."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "paraphrased-evidence-must-reject",
    "type": "strategy",
    "trigger": {
      "family": ["lna"],
      "analysis": ["sizing"],
      "failure_signature": ["band-match-wall"],
      "keywords": ["match", "s11", "band"]
    },
    "evidence": [
      {"quote": "my input match was frequently a little bit off across the band", "source": "my summary impression"}
    ],
    "rule": "Widen the input match network when S11 binds across the band.",
    "applicability": {
      "applies": "Narrowband specs where S11 is the worst margin.",
      "not": "Wideband specs with band-wide S11."
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "malformed-missing-applicability-not",
    "type": "anti-pattern",
    "trigger": {
      "family": ["lna"],
      "analysis": ["sizing"],
      "failure_signature": ["topology-exhaustion"],
      "keywords": ["topology", "reuse"]
    },
    "evidence": [
      {"quote": "HARD FAILURE after escalation; infeasible (closest attempt saved)", "source": "my results notes"}
    ],
    "rule": "Vary the topology class between proposals instead of re-proposing the same archetype after a hard failure.",
    "applicability": {
      "applies": "Tiers where escalation still hard-fails.",
      "not": ""
    }
  }
]
```
